 "notes": "Fiction rule read broadly, following the Tetris/Pac-Man examples: all video game titles and characters were removed (video games, arcade words, esports, word-game apps such as Words With Friends and Wordscapes, Flow Free), plus franchise-specific pickups (Mario mushrooms/shells, Zelda rupee/Triforce, Sonic chaos emerald, Doom/Quake items). Kept Wordle, Connections and Spelling Bee as newspaper puzzles, minesweeper/picross/lights out as generic puzzle types, TV game shows, physical arcade games (Skee-Ball, Whac-A-Mole), real esports events/teams/players, and Polybius (urban legend). 'video games' had only titles and characters; it is now filled with real game companies and studios (flag updated). Toys: kept toy-line brands (Barbie, G.I. Joe, Transformers, My Little Pony, Masters of the Universe, Strawberry Shortcake, Raggedy Ann as public domain) but removed individual cartoon/comic characters (He-Man, Skeletor, Optimus Prime, Jem, Ninja Turtles, Tickle Me Elmo); Warhammer, Gundam and Gunpla removed from model making (Games Workshop kept). Separate: word games mixes board games with puzzles and TV shows, so it does not read as 'table games'; game controls and esports words are generic verbs/sport terms. AFL '50-meter penalty'/'50-meter arc' use American spelling per rule 7 with the Australian form in uk. 'what time is it Mr. Wolf' keeps the UK name in uk (commas are not allowed)."
